## 5. IMPORTANT: REVIEW MANAGEMENT AND GOOGLE POLICY COMPLIANCE

The website must explain the ReviewMattrs feedback and reputation-management workflow accurately.

Businesses need a way to collect private feedback and identify customer complaints before they escalate.

However, Google does not permit review gating, selectively soliciting positive reviews, or suppressing negative reviews.

Therefore:

- Do not claim that ReviewMattrs blocks negative Google reviews.
- Do not promise that negative reviews cannot reach a business's Google profile.
- Do not automatically redirect unhappy customers away from Google while sending satisfied customers to Google.
- Do not present selective review solicitation as a feature.

Instead, communicate the following compliant value proposition:

"Understand customer feedback. Respond faster. Improve every experience."

Design a transparent feedback experience in which every customer has access to the Google review option, alongside an optional private feedback channel.

The SaaS platform can help businesses collect private complaints, identify service issues, monitor public reviews, and respond appropriately.

Present this as a reputation-management and customer-experience improvement system, not a way to manipulate Google ratings.

